  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through Thursday)\nIssued at 1210 AM CDT Fri Oct 16 2026\n\nTemperatures through the weekend and into next week look to steadily \nincrease as a ridge sets up and dominates the upper level synoptic \npattern. A cutoff low will setup over the Southwest US and will work \nwith the ridge to switch our winds from northerly to southwesterly, \naiding in the warm up. By midweek, high temperatures are expected to \nreturn to the upper 70s and low 80s.\n\nA shortwave trough is continuing to be analyzed by some operational \nmodels, bringing a low potential for some spotty showers Tuesday \nafternoon and night. Confidence is low at this time, but low PoPs \nhave been included for that period to reflect the possibility. \nTemperatures also look to decrease upon the passing of this \nshortwave. \n\nOtherwise, the next major weather system being watched is a deep \ntrough that will come off the Pacific Ocean and race eastward. \nCurrent initializations of this system show the Panhandles in a \nfavorable location for precipitation. However, due to how far out \nthis is, exact track and depth of the trough is not very well known \nand will be watched over the next several days.\n\nAbdullayev/Meccariello/Vanden Bosch",
